# Licensing

This repository ships two licences on purpose, and the split is part of the
design rather than an accident of history (PLAN.md, Phase 0).

## The crates — MIT OR Apache-2.0

`crates/xd-core` and `crates/xd-wasm` are dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, at
your option — the Rust norm, dual so that downstream picks. They are the
`.excalidraw` document model: format, geometry, commands, undo. Nothing in them
knows about this application, and nothing in them ever may.

See `crates/xd-core/LICENSE-MIT` and `crates/xd-core/LICENSE-APACHE`.

## The application — PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0

`src-tauri/`, `ui/`, and everything in `ui/standalone/` are licensed under
PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0, matching term.hut. See `LICENSE-POLYFORM`.

## The rule between them

The coupling runs one way only: **the PolyForm application may depend on the
permissive crates; nothing permissive may depend on anything PolyForm.** That
is already the layering the architecture wants, so it costs nothing — but it
does mean `xd-core` can never grow an app-shaped dependency, and
`scripts/check-licenses.sh` asserts it in CI.

## Vendored code

`ui/vendor/` carries third-party ES modules under their own licences, each with
its LICENSE file alongside: Rough.js (MIT) and perfect-freehand (MIT).
